bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-62-| `custody-root` `:288-289` | hot | ''D:'' partition any face-bearing derivation/root by PersonaGroup. ''LEAD:'' prove every remaining use; a node-only secret may enter S only as a separately named row, never by retaining this generic root. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-63-| `keyhive-archive` `:290-291` | hot | ''D:'' split the vessel archive into one identity/archive per PersonaGroup, with no identity above them (`stable-founding-road.mem:203,459`). Node archive row selection is an OPEN JOINT below. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:64:| `veil-archive` `:292-293` | face-hot | ''D:'' the node rests each face's archive at `veil-archive-g<digest of its PersonaGroup>`, so no free index selects it; its FCK arrives with the K15.6 fence. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:65:| `face-atom` `face-atom-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's random atom seed, one per (vessel, PersonaGroup), the device edge's delegate and countersigner and the face's Keyhive Individual. The row's file name carries the SHA-256 digest of its PersonaGroup, so no clear file names a face, and the face-atom custody contract of `@lararium/mesh` (`face-atom-custody.ts`) holds stand, read and keep: absent mints, the same bytes read as a no-op, other bytes refuse as `FaceAtomConflict`. It rests under the vessel key until the K15.6 fence moves it under that face's FCK; it never rides a bundle, a wire or a board. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-66-| `face-atom-ask` `face-atom-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the seed a founding rests before its PersonaGroup exists, named by the digest of the founding's own ask (hearth true name, binding mode, mount flag and compartment); the group row keeps the seed once the group stands and the ask row retires with the bootstrap entry. Same key class and fence as `face-atom`; it never rides a bundle. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-67-| `face-owner` `custody-holder.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's own label, sealed under its custody key: its custody id and the digest of its PersonaGroup. After a face unlocks, the holder compares this row with the floor index entry and refuses by name on a mismatch before it seats anything. Never rides a bundle. |
