bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-73-| `persona-petnames` `node-vessel-identity.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' per-face private name in the face's own row (`.persona-petnames-h<N>.json`); it appears only after that face unlocks. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-74-| `persona-declarations` `node-vessel-identity.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' each face's private declaration (handle, seat claim, chair) in its own row (`.persona-declarations-h<N>.json`). A signed, intentionally public declaration travels by its own published record and never by this row. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:75:| `public-handles` `node-vessel-identity.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the owner mapping of a face's own published record in its own row (`.persona-public-handles-h<N>.json`); public handle bytes ride their own signed record. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-76-| `vessel-face-key` `face-key-custody.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the private face-scoped vessel key rests in the local face whose proof key the scope names, `faces/<fcid>/vessel-face-key-h<N>-<scope digest>.bin`; the founding or join that minted it binds it, and a reader finds it by the scope digest across the face directories (names alone) before that face's key opens it. It stays local, outside a face bundle. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-77-| `face-address-secret` `fleet-join-custody.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the face's fleet address secret rests in that face, `face-address-secret-g<sha256 of its PersonaGroup>.bin`; the name's digest is the group digest the floor index holds. Local unless a defined face recovery route includes it. |
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-84-| `hosting-spent` `hosting-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' per-face replay and spend authority beside its state, `hosting-h<N>/<aid digest>/spent-*`. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-85-| `hosting-carry` `hosting-carry.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the hosting face's rhythm records and the guests' sealed ciphertext rest in that face, `hosting-h<N>/<aid digest>/carry/...`; the walker, a different face, owns the inner ciphertext's content key, and no guest key lands at the host. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:86:| `walk` `node-walk-store.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' the walking face owns its private walk record, `walk-h<N>-<gate digest>.json` in that face; a vessel still walks at one hearth (every face's names are read), and the daemon lists only the unlocked faces' walks. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-87-| `gate-memory` `gate-memory-rows.ts` | face-hot | ''D:'' a gate's withdrawal memory rests in the face whose gate learned it, `gate-memory-h<N>-<subject digest>.bin`; each gate reads and writes only its own face's rows, and another unlocked face's withdrawal reads absent through it. |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-88-| `transition-pending` `seal-ceremony.ts` | floor-plain | ''F:'' field audit: a crossing in progress holds public key-sets, signatures and witnesses and no secret, so it rests in the clear in the seal home (`plain-rows.ts`), readable with no key, written under the custody claim. |
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-100-The worn face is SESSION state: no `active-persona` row rests (the person names the face at each unlock, `lares vault unlock --face N`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-101-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem:102:Rows whose class includes ''LEAD'' block byte movement until their payload and owning principal are proved. Current `face` and `bundle` fields describe filename/export selection only (`vault-carriers.ts:119-165`); they never confer cryptographic separation. The existing S-key rotation sweeps all hot/cold rows (`:64-68,477-510`), so K15 replaces it with per-face and named-S rotation.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-103-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-custody-step-zero.mem-104-<<~/ahu>>
