bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-30-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:31:* ''One KEL grammar.'' `packages/lararium-mesh/src/vessel-kel.ts` follows the house grammar (stable AID, `seq`, predecessor digest, event digest from the canonical core, strict fold, forks surfaced) with place authority alone: one key, no guardians, no quorum, no interaction events.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-32-* ''Inception.'' `{kind, t:"icp", seq:0, key, next}`: `key` seats the ONLINE signer, `next` commits the digest of the cold key under `PLACE_NEXT_KEY_DOMAIN`, and the signer signs the event itself. The AID is the inception's digest.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-33-* ''Rotation.'' `{kind, t:"rot", aid, seq, prev, reveal, key, next}`: `reveal` opens the prior event's commitment, `key` seats the replacement signer, `next` commits a fresh cold key, and the REVEALED cold key signs. The online signer never selects its successor. A reused commitment or key refuses.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-34-* ''The card ceremony.'' The cold key rests on a founding card alone: its seed reaches no file. A founding and every rotation read the card back through an injected `PlaceFoundingCard` before a byte lands (the CLI adapts `cold-card-readback`; a staged test root stands in). A rotation runs under one custody claim: verify the card against the head, mint the next cold key and the replacement signer, read the replacement card back, stage the signed event with the replacement signer durably (`.vessel-rotating*.json`), publish the chain and the key file, remove the stage. A restart reconciles a staged file against the last verified head and never invents a successor; a staged file with no read-back card, or of another head, refuses.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:35:* ''Peers learn the head.'' Rows ride the Nexus carriage board under `PLACE_KEL_PREFIX` keyed by the inception AID (`place-kel-board.ts`), and the carry bundle carries them to an offline herm (`carry-bundle.ts`, `placeKel`). A reader pins the inception, `foldPlaceKel` verifies every digest, sequence, predecessor, reveal and cold signature to the head, and `acceptPlaceHead` holds it against the last accepted head. A gap, rollback or fork refuses advancement; the last accepted head stays "as of my last sync". A row that fails its own signature never advances a head.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:36:* ''The framed duties.'' The five floor duties (carriage carrier, place floor pin, flow pointer, raise challenge, gate place finish) sign and verify one image `u32 len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` (`frameFloorDuty`, `floorDutyOf`, `verifyPlaceDuty`, `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead` in `place-signer.ts`). The KEL events sign under the KEL grammar, never a sixth floor domain.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:37:* ''The seed census.'' `tools/seed-census.mjs` names every raw-seed consumer against an explicit list, proves itself on a planted consumer, and fails on any new consumer or stale entry. The K15 entries ride it as named owed exceptions in `{rule, file, match, count, reason}` shape, and K15 burns each when its bond lands.
