bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-48-# ''Built ~ the carry bundle'' (`carry-bundle.ts`; `carry-bundle-place-kel.test`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-49-# ''Built ~ the seed census'' (`tools/seed-census{.mjs,.test.mjs,-witness.sh}`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:50:# ''Built ~ the browser founding'' (`browser-vessel-identity.ts`: `foundBrowserPlaceKel`, `loadBrowserPlaceKel`, `readBrowserPlaceHead`). A leaf mints the armed inception through the same mesh grammar and reads its cold card back through the same `PlaceFoundingCard` port (`place-founding-card.ts` in mesh). A leaf holds no floor, so with no ceremony seated the identity open founds the device key and no KEL, and the explicit door refuses `PlaceFoundingCardUnread` until a ceremony UI seats a card (`placeFoundingCard` on `openBrowserVessel`). Heads read through the one `foldPlaceKel`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-51-# ''Built ~ the genesis paths.'' Node `runInit`, the hearth founding, the herm's cold kindle (`bulb-kindle.test`) and both cofounders' places each mint the armed chain through the real founding door.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-52-# ''Built ~ the rotate door.'' `lares vessel rotate` (`commands/rotate-place.ts`) reads the old card on a terminal, prints and reads back the replacement through the same port, refuses beside a standing vessel, and leaves reconcile of a cut-short stage to the node (`vessel-rotate-door.test`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:53:# ''Built ~ the fold bound.'' `foldPlaceKel` drops foreign and unsigned rows before any digest walk, caps the signed rows it walks at `PLACE_KEL_ROWS_PER_AID`, and carries at most `PLACE_KEL_FORK_EVIDENCE` competing successors from the first fork seq.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:54:# ''Owed ~ the readers by head.'' The four duty verifiers verify under the key a caller passes; the floor pin claim lane (W14 to W16) resolves each duty's signer through `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`. Names that key a place by its inception key follow the head when that lane lands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem-55-# ''Owed ~ the gate place finish.'' `gate-exchange.ts` already frames its image and did not move.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane.mem:56:# ''Owed ~ K15's bonds.'' The vessel-wide Keyhive Individual and place card, the bare place leaf, the relay key, daemon auth, device and face work, internal asks and `lares meme` signing stay on the seed census as named K15 exceptions.
