bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-55-* ''CI'' (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`): `gh run list --branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5` names the run for the pushed head; a later commit waits for the next push. `held-out.yml` runs on every push to a feature branch and to `main`, weekly, and by hand (`gh workflow run held-out.yml --ref <branch>`). It builds the product image once, runs one hosted job per cell (`node tools/held-out-cells.mjs cells` names them: each whole driver, and each scenario `tools/mesh-scenarios.sh --list` names), and its merge job prints one `HELD-OUT-DRIVER:` line per driver and one `HELD-OUT-VERIFY:` line. A cell that never answered reads red there by name. `node tools/held-out-steps.mjs <cell>` runs one cell's job on a desk, read off the workflow.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-56-* ''The docker mesh'' (by hand): `crossing-witness`; `node tools/mesh-pins.mjs --up` stands the mesh pinned; `herm-mesh-witness` carries `node/alpha` across three hops; `mesh-scenarios nexus` (`tools/mesh-scenarios.sh --list` names every scenario and starts no build; `MESH_PROJECT` names the run's own compose project). The mesh publishes `MESH_PORT_*` on loopback, every node service requires `LARES_HARNESS_IMAGE`, and `tools/harness-image.sh` checks its digest. A hearth whose log carries a `[lararium] fatal:` line reads as not stood.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:57:* ''Island doors'': `tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` measures which vessel doors (fetch · rest · custody write · dyad) each island of the node and web assemblies reaches on the built tree, and every source call that spawns an island or attaches it a door, against the committed table `tools/capability-inventory.json`. The table measures reach, never a door's policy (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor#/the-harnesses">>). A door a class reaches where the table says it did not, a new or extra seam, a seam that left or a new ask reads red by name; a deliberate change re-writes the table in the commit that makes it (`node tools/capability-inventory.mjs --write`). A browser wiki or session island reaches no door and meets the dyad refusal; the browser's daemon island reads `unmeasured`, since its spawn seam stands inside `openBrowserVessel`; a session island's view asks run through the pool core's own listener, which no row drives.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-58-* ''The red register'': `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/unbuilt-laws.test.ts` declares each law the models imply and no code enforces; `tools/unbuilt-laws-witness.sh` reports a declared red that greened.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:59:* ''Known environmental reds'': `lararium-tw5` `tests/syncer-back-parity.e2e.test.ts` (Chromium legs) and `tests/meme-routes.e2e.test.ts` fail where no browser or server socket stands; the browser suite reads `no tests` under a `HOME` that holds no Playwright Chromium.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-60-* ''The operator's live `~/.lares` vessel'' holds an earlier shape that this build refuses. Never stand it here; it takes the fresh start, by hand (#/fresh-start).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-61-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-62-!!! Steps
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:63:# `export LAR_ROOT=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any in-tree boot or any `lares` command that touches the store. `LAR_ROOT` moves the store, the bags root and every projection mirror root; `LAR_BAGS` alone moves only the bags root, and the projection still writes the tracked `bags/` and `wikis/`. A staged e2e vessel takes its own scratch `LAR_ROOT` and no global `LAR_BAGS`. One `lares meme normalize|check` reads files and needs only a scratch `LAR_BAGS`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-64-# `LAR_ROOT` leaves these homes where they stand: `~/.mempalace` (the destructive `mempalace repave` among its readers), `~/.venv`, `~/.local/bin`, and the harness homes `~/.claude`, `~/.codex`, `~/.copilot`. A `vessel stand --codex` under a scratch root still writes the operator's real harness home.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-65-# Build: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` only where a lead approved an install, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob that `head-parity` and the plugin smoke need), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`. A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules; populate them before building there.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-66-# ''A founding wants a human route on a TTY.'' With no TTY it refuses `CredentialTtyRefusal`, and no flag or environment variable carries a credential. A harness founds through the test door: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs` stages the root, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs` names the published test route, then `lares vessel found --skip-build`; `tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs` opens a marked scratch root. An agent may read vessel state and hand the operator the next founding command as text; the operator performs each founding and custody act.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:67:# ''Every boot rests at the floor.'' A verb that needs sovereign state refuses at a standing floor and names `lares vault unlock`. A harness that reads the first `gate key:` line of a log reads the carriage relay's key where a relay stands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-68-# ''The container'': `tools/lares-container.sh` offers `up`, `down`, `found` and `logs` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor">>). ''The browser surface'': `tools/browser-ci.sh` over `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`, one project and image tag per builder (`BROWSER_CI_PROJECT`, `BROWSER_CI_IMAGE`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:69:# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) rides in git and must equal a fresh build: rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it. `genesis/` carries that bundle, the boot shadows and the engine blob by address, and the wiki inside a founded vessel runs the bytes genesis carries; a bake (`pnpm --filter @lararium/node build:genesis`) lands as its own labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` commit with the CAS change, and a vessel founded on the earlier seed re-founds. `tools/genesis-parity-witness.sh` reads the gap: a bundle that runs ahead of genesis reads red until a bake closes it or a row in `genesis/unbaked.json` declares it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-70-# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the ignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-71-# Crew shape: the work swarm, one Sonnet Episkopos with one Sol and one Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` seat, the Opus controller reading every chunk (its seats and the fallback stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-shapes), five rounds per set at most, and the solo chain runs beside as many side lanes as hold disjoint files. A builder returns a patch on a narrow one-module brief; the lead applies, builds, tests and commits in its own worktree, then lands whole commits with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>` after rebuilding the touched `dist`, since the commit hook runs the built CLI. A lead copies its resume sheet out of the session scratch directory after each commit: a restart empties that directory.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-72-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-73-!!! The standing law that bites ~ read the carrier before arguing with it
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:74:* ''The frame stands as canon'': DOCTYPE, the SOH bearing, STX, `toml meta` first in the body, the body, ETX with its `ni:///sha-256;…` check, EOT. One span per carrier; a spelling outside the frame grammar tears the frame (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext-framing">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-75-* ''The frame's `?` and the gate's unechoed key stay distinct.'' `from="?"` declares an unresolved bearing at the grammar layer; the gate withholds a known key at the transport layer. Their one shared law reads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/system-pattern-integrities#/threshold-pattern-integrities">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:76:* ''Ingest decides from a parse and a verdict.'' The deserializer stands as the pure meme-to-tiddlers function; `verdict()` (Match · Stale · Absent · Torn · Bare) lives in `@lararium/memetic-frame`; checks live in `carrier-check.ts`, repairs in normalize, policy at each door. A stale check on a human edit warns; a torn frame refuses; text with no frame reads as bare data, never a meme.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-77-* ''Never refuse on the stock syncer path''; surface on the alert rail (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/syncer-back-parity">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-78-* ''The quoteblock floor fences at two grains'': the whole chunk inside the deserializer, and a child's body in place at the child gate (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/ahu#/quoteblock-floor">>).
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-81-* ''Grounds before wins'': rank work by what inherits shape from what, never by confidence in the next wire (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures#/grounds-before-wins">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-82-* ''One holder per store, one Lararium per human'': a second holder meets `StoreHeld` across containers and namespaces (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:83:* ''Fragments'': every `lar:` fragment roots at `#/…`, one raw `#`, `/` nests, `$` reserved (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/memetic-wikitext">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-84-* ''Grammar lives in the tiddlers'' (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-*.tid` generate `grammar-table.generated.ts`); sigil heads stay core ASCII; `aka` pins as information, `kanawai` pins as binding, `kahea` transcludes live.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:85:* ''Early alpha'': no back-compat, no shims, no legacy recovery; a stale thing aligns to the current frame and grammar, and a third human's arrival ends that line (#/rulings, the fence) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/wild-bytes">>). Derive, never enumerate. One function, one relation.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-86-* ''A registry compiled about subjects refuses at any scope'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-87-* ''A relation's evidence keeps its type'' and ''a worker keeps its own storage scope'': <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/causal-island#/selected-contracts">>.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-105-* ''All CODE runs dockerized''; the host keeps only the hooks into the operator's environment (files and bags, session capture, the editor and CLI entry, custody).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-106-* ''ONE Lararium per HUMAN, never per face.'' A human's faces keep their data together in one vessel (`PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one`); the recorded face-switch act carries plurality. No design assumes a container or a state mount per face.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:107:* ''A SESSION wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator-ruled; quote license: //"a human might want a tab open as one Persona, and a tab open as another Persona... same vessel. Identity as relation."// and //"a CLI session wears its own face too … those act as ephemeral UX"//). A vessel holds its roots and one store. A session — a browser tab, a CLI run — contracts in as ONE persona, and several sessions may live at once over one vessel, each wearing its own. Every act carries exactly one face. Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire: each session proves itself under its own face-scoped key, never under a key the vessel shares across them. The vessel-wide parts (custody, the daemon island) serve every session and let none read another's planes.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-108-* ''Local-first first.'' Cloud "backup larariums" under other humans' delegated keys stand DEFERRED until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface. Nothing in the container or the face-switch work may foreclose a keyless ciphertext carrier later.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-109-* ''The boundary'' (settled by the house under those rulings): one multi-arch image; `/workspace` mounts bags and wikis, `/state` mounts vessel homes and custody, never an image layer; the local socket stays INSIDE the container and the host CLI enters through `docker compose exec`; the app never receives the docker socket; mDNS offers unauthoritative LAN candidates and a pinned admission alone grants authority; DNS-01 wildcard TLS supplies browser secure contexts; a release manifest binds the image digest to the genesis, engine and grammar CIDs.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-117-* ''A household seed serves its holder alone.'' A one-operator seed gives durable use without recruiting a mesh; useful local standing precedes every wider relation.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-118-* ''Guests walk the household seed.'' Planes stay persona-scoped, so a guest sees its own documents, the public and infrastructure shelf, and every realm its worn face stands in; a face may stand in many, as a person belongs to many clubs, and a guest's other faces stand in none of them.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:119:* ''Add-a-face (A).'' The daemon writes the public half; the terminal seals the recovery share; seating stays a separate act.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-120-* ''Every leaf starts at the floor with its own root.'' A human may later JOIN a leaf to a PersonaGroup so its devices sync as one fleet; joining never takes the device's own root away.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-121-* ''Founding persona zero belongs to standing'', never to a later verb. A capable vessel founds its household seed, so a "vessel with no charter" reads Mu.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-133-* ''Names and counters'': a counter orders one writer's own emissions only, and the face lives at the session capability. The per-Nexus convergence secret and its keyring leave the model: nothing derives from one, the Stable founding act yields none, no seat act commits to one and no admission delivers one. (operator ruling; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/cap-tier#/key-delivery">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-134-* ''Kahu acts fall into four chartered classes'': ordinary (1-of-1); high-impact — charter, admission, trust root (3-of-5, or 2-of-3 for a small body); emergency (2-of-3, a narrow pre-authorized power reviewed by a later causal act); revocation (the threshold of the original act). A challenge appends to the record and may pause LOCAL reliance; it never halts the protocol. Admission of a Kahu or a Lamplighter always takes the seat quorum, and no ordinary single-seat class covers it; kapae and rolls take the quorum too; the user road rides its own bound (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/seed-and-nexus">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:135:* ''Renewal runs as three sequences, kept apart'' (the realm feed, a per-renewal causal position, the KEL), and lapse arrives as three distinct events: signed departure, recorded removal by relation-scoped kapae, renewal supersession.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:136:* ''A cancel crossing a herm yields three receipts'': the caller's abandonment, the relay's delivery (transit only), the vessel's outcome. A caller timeout never counts as a cancel; eviction answers `retention-gap`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-137-* ''One face at a time names WHO ANSWERS for an act.'' The switch law reads in `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy#/one-face`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-138-* ''A session wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator ruling).
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-144-* ''The floor key keeps the vessel's public name''; the sealed custody root derives the veil and the sovereign caps. The veil change stays destroy-class.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-145-* ''Unbind offers an S-key rotation loudly'', every time, never folded in silently.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:146:* ''Locality law'': an unattended ember answers on the local link only, and only where the hearth holds a hardware freshness anchor the ember checks on each ask (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest); a relay pin wants an attending hand. The vessel rests at the floor and raises when t embers answer; the raise lapses by non-renewal, which reads as the raise's next causal boundary (#/rulings, how a raise lapses).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-147-* ''HOT ⊥ COLD'': S key and keyhive state stay hot; the root, the recovery shares and the next-root seed unwrap per act.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-148-* Measuring hardware x-only ECDH (phone enclaves) before trusting an enclave-held ember: approved, deferred.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-173-* ''No guardians on the day'': each face starts one-of-one on its own paper, and enrolment comes later by one typed first-enrolment event the face's own current key signs on its own log.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-174-* ''Shore saves, as built'': a rename onto a standing title proceeds as an ordinary write at field grain; a tombstone moved into a bag that lacks the title refuses unless the hand asks to shadow.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:175:* ''A seat gets ADDED, never replaced.'' The long-span act adds a holder to BOTH cabals — a Kahu seat and a Lamplighter contract — and the founders keep their chairs; one founding Kahu may hold seats across many Nexuses. The road proves the roll that adds a seat, and the new holder's carriage contract, first. A passed chair stays a possible act. A Kahu who works far from the other seats needs a co-signature for every quorum act, so the partial-and-cosign door carries a partial act across a relay and back with no clock.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-176-* ''Per-Nexus identifiers'': an admit names a per-Nexus identifier, a random leaf no other Nexus can link. The face's lineage may re-issue it by a signed hand-over the gate verifies, and per-Nexus keys mint at random, never from the persona seed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:177:* ''Every boot rests at the floor until a human unlocks'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor">>). At the floor every fleet lane stays shut, and the custody write door, the rest door and the dyad door answer the daemon island alone. A bounded ember stays design input: it raises to SERVING alone, never signs or admits, runs on a count and never a clock, needs the device's own unlock plus a second signal, records each raise, and any other device of the human removes it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-178-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-179-!!! The models, each in its own carrier (operator rulings, approved as presented)
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-180-* ''Full models land early'': #/the-attractor.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-181-* ''One roadmap'': this carrier. Standing procedures rest at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/working-procedures">>, and the grammar watch at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/grammar-watch">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:182:* ''The sealed store'': cleartext lives in the live wiki and the operator's projected files alone. Private bytes take randomized authenticated sealing addressed over the ciphertext; the private tier takes no convergent sealing, and no opener returns unauthenticated bytes. A content key carries a version and rolls at a causal removal act. History at admission must have stood declared when written, and one logical bag name carries its key-roll epochs (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-183-* ''The backup bundle'': a bundle holds ONE face, sealed under a route the person holds, and carries that face's root with its own lines and no key of any seat. Its memory rides as content keys, sealed inside the key island: a bundle opens every surviving value ever sealed under a version it carries, values written after its cut included, and no version minted later. A restore runs as a recovery act that takes a fresh veil and a new seat, and one face on a new device reads as the same audience for the versions that face already held (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-184-* ''Removal's reach'': four edges take a marker (dyad, vouch, member, carriage). A vouch edge answers to its voucher and to a chartered quorum; a seal roll carries every shadow; a standing shadow reaches every gate and drives a key roll; a contested tie keeps the shadow up; mutual removal ends in an explicit fork (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/four-edges">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-185-* ''The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group'', so a seat's revocation rolls the key of every bag the group reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>; a fresh group stays owed, `K12` of #/the-loops).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-186-* ''The hands'': every hand opens a session. A tasked spirit comes down to an AI, a Mask and the vessel's seat, attended or standing; the vessel's own key serves as a spirit's system identity; a Mask counts as no pet-name. The door carries and the hand authorizes, over one verb table, and a standing seat never signs an act that changes who holds authority (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:187:* ''Sealed-row acts ride the custody door'', never a store verb whose output lands in the daemon's document in the clear (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-188-* ''Gate keys come in three tiers'': a floor route's keys derive from the floor key, and a sovereign route's from the sealed custody root (operator ruling); the serving route's bundle derives from SK, a third tier that leaves those two untouched (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate). A faceless place takes a fourth arm at the gate, the place arm, and a session opens before its certificate. The floor key rests outside the vessel key, and the face proof names what a holder of the disk without the passphrase reaches and never reaches (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-189-* ''The widget render boundary stands withdrawn'', and the parser carries recovery (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/graceful-parsing">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-190-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-191-!!! Operator rulings, 2026-10-16 ~ approved as the controller's story leans
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:192:* ''A joined device reads the hearth's corpus and keeps its own.'' A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, and its writes stay in its own; the oracle plane (the hearth's catalog, daemon doc and faces' planes) never crosses (`device-admit.ts#admitCanonDocs`). Row `W21` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-193-* ''The bag plane hides its creator before strangers carry it.'' The carried bag event's creator identifier in the clear gets measured red-first and ranked before wave three: ahead of anything that lets a third human's data cross a herm. Row `W25`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-194-* ''An agent's dissent drafts; a person's ask edits'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract">> #/the-hands): an agent never overrides a person's edit, and a person's direct ask to edit a tiddler makes the edit the person's own act, bounded by the ask and the asker's authority.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:195:* ''The system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-16). Only each Nexus's Kahu cabal writes the `lares` and `lararium` wikis and bags live. Every other wiki, and every other hand, mounts them read-only by CID: the latest release that cabal approved. The release rides the Nexus's crossroads board as its public answer, naming the floor CID under the Kahu steward's seal. The cabal approves the exact bytes under its charter's threshold, and a herm carries the answer without signing it. Every wiki mounts that floor through `@oracle`, which never writes. A vessel moves its floor pin only when it accepts a newer signed release. With no Nexus speaking, it stands on its last accepted floor, or on genesis. A face's wikis follow the floor of the Nexus that face stands in, so one vessel may hold two floors and never ties its faces together. An edit aimed at the floor copies up into the wiki's own working layer, and an offering back travels as a draft into the cabal's realm. A lone hearth is a Nexus of one, so its operator stands as its own Kahu. Row `W26` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-196-* DreamDOM's ruled questions stand in <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom">> #/open-rulings.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-197-
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-201-* ''On the node, the boot marks the unlock and the session marks the face'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house reading). The per-tab ask binds browser tabs; a node unlocks once per boot through its custody door, and every CLI run, MCP seat and watcher proves its own face at the gate without asking again (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/session-unlock-2026">> #/the-node-scope).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-202-* ''The last tab closes, and the browser rests at its floor'' (operator, 2026-10-18, approving the house lean). The unlock lives in page memory alone, so the browser vessel's sovereign composition ends with its last tab and the next tab asks again. Row `B1`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:203:* ''One Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup, none above them'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"it's the only way to retain control over faces that don't know about each other"//). Each face's PersonaGroup owns its Keyhive identity, its event store, its registry, its archive and its content-key seat; no vessel-wide identity registers a face's bags, delegates them, or holds a face's group. Two faces of one vessel then never link on the wire, a removal from one face rolls that face's bags alone, and a bundle restores one face and nothing of another. Today the vessel's own identity registers every bag and delegates each face's bags through itself, and the vessel and every face share one event store and one content-key holder (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/keyhive-per-persona-group-2026">>). House readings under the operator's confidence, each naming what flips it: a herm keeps a floor-only transport key, behind a red test that it can neither author, resolve nor observe a face's capabilities, and holds no Keyhive identity if that test fails; several face hives share one process only after a substrate probe reads them isolated, and each face's hive runs in its own worker otherwise; co-mingled history migrates by fresh identities and an old mixed archive refuses by name, with no bridge; a founder that cannot leave its group leaves by a fresh PersonaGroup. Row `K15` carries the build, folding `W25` and `K12`; `W26`'s slice 3 waits on its face context.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:204:* ''A cabal shares through the faces its members choose'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18, on the Teshima Family Council story). Kalani founds a private family council; Leilani, already standing on the DreamNet with several faces, chooses which of them join it, and a face she keeps back never learns the council exists. The council's hive reads as a Keyhive group with no key of its own: its members act through their own faces' identities, so nothing stands above them, and a presentation reads valid against the current set without naming which member made it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/identity-classes">> #/the-handle-chain). Any current member's face promotes into the council's canon; a graft takes the threshold; a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` at the threshold or a fork that omits the captor (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">> #/the-unswept-corner); members read the owner-set as faces, never as humans. A private council declares no heraldry and lives in its members' address books under pet-names (cabal-realm #/heraldry). Row `K16` carries the story as `K15`'s acceptance.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:205:* ''The asker seals'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, F6's custody fork). Once the browser holder owns the Repo and the daemon kernel, it routes each sealed write to the admitted tab whose session caused it, else to any admitted, unlocked tab of that write's face; with no awake admitted tab, the write waits, named `seal-awaits-session`, never silent and never decided by a clock. No key material leaves a tab, and each sealer holds the row-class key the occupied carrier's overwrite proof opens. A SharedWorker carries no promise to run while its tabs freeze, and no `MessagePort` event reports a peer's death (round one, 2026-10-19), so a seal that waits names its wait.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:206:* ''A face's custody rows seal under its own key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Each PersonaGroup holds an independent random face custody key (FCK) that only its own slot tree opens (passphrase, paper or PRF), never wrapped under the vessel key, so a holder of the S key or of another face's unlock opens none of its rows. Face-private rows: each face's veil archive, face-key custody, guardian sets, face-provisional, the fleet-join address secret and record, a pending join bound to its target face, the per-face device shares, and each face's partition of the handle book and roster; the vessel Keyhive archive splits per PersonaGroup under `K15`. A face bundle carries that face's identity, archive, FCK recovery route and guardian set, and nothing of a sibling. Today every hot and cold custody row seals under one S key (`vault-carriers.ts`, `browser-custody.ts`), so face isolation reads as routing alone until this lands. Row `K15` carries the build, and `F6` slice three lands with its step 3. How a vessel-common act unlocks dissolves (next ruling).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:207:* ''A shared act never makes a shared secret'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; four ratcheted research rounds, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">>). Every act that touches more than one face sorts one of three ways: its private bytes DISSOLVE into the owning face's rows (D), its public bytes stand at the FLOOR by design (F), or it names a vessel SECRET (S) whose principal and opener the house names row by row. A mixed carrier splits before it sorts. The browser holds no vessel key: founding, fleet join, slot changes, roster, archives, handle book, dyads, restore and clear sort D or F, so each tab asks only its own face's unlock and public floor work asks nothing. Phones, installed web apps, probes, the CLI, MCP and watcher seats and a native shell hold no S. A tablet waking floor carries ciphertext and public rows unattended and decrypts no face's row. A container restarts at its floor and nothing unlocks it unattended. A guest island that owns a key store stands as its own vessel. A node holds S only for rows it names: the serving key has no row yet, so it guards nothing today. * ''The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19; a fifth research round, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/custody-per-face-2026">> #/the-place-signer). A node's place identity keeps a KEL whose inception commits the next key, and that next key rides the founding card beside the seed charter's cold next key, offline; the online place signer runs unattended for an enumerated allowlist of floor duties alone (the KEL's own events excepted, which the card's key signs), rests under the host's TPM-bound credential where the host offers one and an owner-only file elsewhere, and never rides an environment, an image or a log. A stolen online signer rotates away by the card; a lost card beside a stolen signer re-founds. The floor holds no custody key; it holds its own named place signer. The format change rides the founding bake (`X0`). The place KEL commits its next cold key on the founding card and rotates by that card (`W29`), and the seed census names every reach of the seed past the floor, K15's owed bonds among them (`tools/seed-census.mjs`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:208:* ''Custody and identity read by capability, never by host'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19: //"I consider node and browser isomorphic-by-intent. Eventually, a browser-vessel somewhere may grow comparable capabilities to a node vessel, and this pattern cascades outwards to all future vessels."//). Three rules hold on every vessel, present and planned: a vessel meets each face through that face's atom alone, its veil signing every dial, join, enrolment, sibling channel and daemon proof made on that face's behalf, never one device-wide key; a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor, for the floor's allowlisted duties, under the pre-rotated place KEL; and a faceless vessel reading another's floor proves nothing private, reading the public shelf under the floor card's pin. A node's daemon auth, device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today (`open-node-vessel.ts`), and a browser's do the same (`open-browser-vessel.ts`); each is a bond owed, carried by `K15`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-209-* ''Identity enacts a bond'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19). Lineage stays within a root, and covenant joins roots: a root (a compartment seed, a vessel key, a face custody key, a charter seat, a content key) derives children for its own duties alone, and any identity spanning two roots is a bond, an act both ends sign that seats a fresh key of its own, resting with the end whose privacy it serves and lapsing by its own act; no closure holds a root (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/identity-enacts-relation">> #/identity-as-bond, its seven laws and bond table).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-210-* ''A face's device veil is its own random key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-19, re-reading the 2026-09-05 veil ruling). Each PersonaGroup's veil on a device mints at random when the device joins that face and rests under that face's FCK, so no device seed stands as an ancestor of any face's veil; it stays vessel-local, never presents, and reads mint-shaped to every observer. The group-secret opener follows it.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-212-* ''A write lands on a working layer, and canon takes it by promotion'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18). A `LOAD` lands on a wiki's working slot alone; canon takes content only by the cap-gated promotion `MOVE` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">>), and genesis and founding seed canon through their own named door. An act aimed at a wiki no island mounts asks the vessel to mount it, and refuses gracefully, naming the cause, when the mount cannot stand. Row `W27` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-213-* ''Every bag opens as its own wiki'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18). The floor recipe names the bag alone over `@oracle`, derived and never minted, and an absent record reads as that floor, never as "no such wiki"; a composed wiki's record, which a hand authors, lays several bags and plugin offerings beneath the wiki's own canon bag (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">> #/quine). No act enumerates bags to mint wikis. Row `W27` carries the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:214:* ''One owner per registry; the floor reads by CID'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-18: //"Architecture stands, leans stand"//). The `@oracle` document as a registry every vessel writes retires: one id carried one `lares` and one `lararium` pointer for the whole fleet, and a joined vessel's pointer replaced its hearth's, a shape a two-vessel probe and three shard runs measured. `@oracle` stands as the floor's read-face over a manifest CID, which a wiki mounts read-only by the pin its face accepted. Each registry carries only what its scope's owner writes: a vessel's bootstrap holds its own document pointers and its accepted floor pins; `@catalog` the operator's documents; the Kahu realm the live `lares` and `lararium` documents and their drafts; the crossroads board the Nexus's one public answer. The leans the ruling adopts: the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, with `bags/` projected on the Kahu's vessel alone; a one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group, so one predicate decides every hand's reach into system canon; the release answer, the Nexus's one public answer, names the Nexus AID, the charter epoch, the release before it and the floor manifest CID, sealed by the steward, with the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes riding attached; a vessel records an accepted release as a sealed hot row per (face, Nexus) that only a person's act moves; genesis bakes the first floor, a corpus CID in the seed. A signing domain of its own carries the release, `floor-release`, so no seal over another shape verifies as one (operator-approved, 2026-10-18). The shape and its slices stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>; rows `W26`, `W21` and `P8` carry the build.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-215-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-216-!!! House rulings under the operator's delegation ~ the questions the operator delegated, each with what flips it
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-220-* ''How a raise lapses'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A raise lives one boot and lapses at the next causal boundary (a lock, a restart, a human unlock, a counted removal), and that boundary IS the expiry the waking floor requires; no timer and no heartbeat ends a standing, and the count spends at the raise ledger's durable commit before SERVING composes, so a crash before the commit spends nothing and serves nothing and a crash after it burns the raise. The reason: quiet never tells a slow device from a gone one; the residue: a rolled-back ledger on a disk copy restores spent raises. The ruling flips on a causal renewal event every reader receives that also survives the ember's loss (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/waking-floor#/the-shape">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-221-* ''A removal no reader can keep'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). The based removal refuses by name where no parallel-drafts reader keeps the concurrent words, or every reader failed, and the store authors nothing; the refusal carries a durable conflict handle (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), so a hand whose editor went offline finds the same conflict on its return. The reason: a draft the store wrote would choose a bag, a tier and a steward no hand named. The ruling flips on an already-authorized destination for such words that keeps provenance and tier without the store choosing either (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:222:* ''The outbox at rest'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each outbox parcel seals under randomized authenticated encryption with a stable outbox key the vessel key wraps and an unlock hands the daemon island, the way content keys reach it, and rests under a random name with its routing inside the sealed body, so a locked disk names no reader; the `sealed-outbox` row leaves `floor-plain` for a sealed class. Before a parcel's atomic commit nothing stands sendable, after it the parcel re-opens and retries at the next unlock, and after a ship and before the local delete the receiver folds a repeat idempotently. The reason: a reader digest on a stolen disk names a relationship; no flip stands expected, since the ruling closes a residue (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:223:* ''The herm relay leg'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). The ask rides the sealed sibling session under that session's seal with a tagged inner frame, and the delivery receipt stays a bare session note good for the asker alone, bound to a unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; reach narrows to one PersonaGroup, and the leg lands with `W9`. The reason: the fewest new shapes, and no signing domain minted for a transport fact. The ruling flips on a concrete need for a third party to audit relay delivery after the asker vanishes (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-224-* ''The disk watcher's reach'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A pending removal settles with no person present only under a standing instruction the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag and a bounded class of removals (a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling): the watcher executes within it, every settled removal lands in the audit with the instruction it rode, and `lares shore restore` still answers it. An automated seat never signs one, a standoff (disk and records differ) never settles without a person, and a mass vanish past the instruction's ceiling stays pending for a person. The reason: a person who answered in writing for exactly that class has answered, and a count alone proves no intent; the ruling flips on a single incident where an in-scope instruction deleted what a person meant to keep (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-225-* ''The restore's key history'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A restored face stands PROVISIONAL until at least one party to its relation (a sibling device of the same human, a seated chair of its Nexus, or a guardian) shows its own log view and that view agrees with the restore's head; while provisional the face reads, recovers and serves its own content and signs no authority-changing act, the restore prints which head it read and from where, and the provisional state names who could confirm it. Where every such party stays unreachable, the guardians' recovery path (the impersonation quorum) answers, never the local read alone. The reason: no vessel reads a head it never received, and the house keeps no registry of heads; no flip stands, and the residue stays stated: one agreeing party may itself sit stale (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-226-* ''The Offering Antigen scope'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A signed Offering act carries a stable scope, the joint Nexus AID its signed inception mints, beside `sealEpochCid` as the authorizing epoch. The receiver resolves its own charter scope, verifies the act's epoch inside that scope's locally held lineage, checks the quorum at that exact epoch, and only then folds; an act whose scope differs stays as foreign evidence outside the `kapae` and `un_kapae` fold, and an incomplete lineage reads `unavailable`. The joint inception image commits to the offer fingerprint and to both founders' fresh cold successor commitments, and a successor commitment a vault already used refuses, so the AID names one founding statement and two foundings by one roster never alias. The reason: a neighbour's condemnation copied onto another board reads as testimony, never as that board's verdict. The ruling flips on a case where two foundings by one roster must read as one Nexus (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/offering-antigen-scope-decision-record">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:227:* ''The fork-resolve act'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). A fork stays a fork, and every reader names the branch it follows; no clock, no longest chain and no third-party quorum picks a branch. Two acts resolve one. ABANDON: a seal record a branch's own quorum signs at its head, closing that branch for every reader who holds it, erasing nothing and touching no sibling. REUNION: one canonical image naming the scope AID, both held heads sorted, and the new seats, threshold and successor commitments, signed by each branch's quorum at its head over identical bytes; the verifier proves both heads inside the same AID's lineages from a common ancestor, and the record becomes the common head. A seal record's predecessors form a sorted set of one or two, built before the fence; until the reunion verifier lands, a two-predecessor record refuses `REUNION_UNBUILT`. The reason: a split household reunites only by a paper both halves sign. The ruling flips on a fork that neither branch's quorum can still sign for.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-228-* ''The re-seal proof'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). When a content key rolls at a counted removal, the face session that writes each replacement signs one causal re-seal record per replacement: the bag locator, the old and new key-version ids, the old and new ciphertext addresses, the logical entry it replaces and the removal act that authorized the roll. The removal quorum signs the roll, never each body. A reader with partial history verifies the signature and every binding it holds, and reports a missing parent as unverified, never as complete. The format lands with sealed-store step three, before the fence. The reason: a phone offline through the roll needs to know which photo replaced which, and whose hand re-sealed it. The ruling flips on proof that the key-version record, manifests and checkpoints already show every replacement and omission to both kinds of reader (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-229-* ''Guardian enrolment's shape'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each face founds one-of-one with no guardians, and its log's verifier knows a typed first-enrolment event from the start: the face's own current key signs it, it commits the guardian set and threshold, and the face's prefix stays as it stands; every later change to the set takes the guardians' authority. The event shape and its verifier land before the fence, so an enrolment never re-founds a face. The reason: a face founded alone keeps its Handle's history when guardians join a year later, and no third hand holds standing over a one-of-one face. The ruling flips on an existing event kind that already permits that first, face-key-signed transition. Guardian count, request authentication, the veto, death and succession stay open (#/open).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:230:* ''Engine cadence'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Cadence keeps its own lineage and threshold, apart from every seat key. A Nexus's joint founding cites one cadence inception that names each founder's hearth, the device that bears the reboot, as a holder; a household seed carries none, since its one holder bears its reboots. Each hearth mints its cadence key at random on the device, never derived from serving or floor material, and keeps it, with its next-key commitment, as a `cold` row under the vessel key that unwraps per act; no sixth custody class and no extra card at the founding. A holder may later rotate onto a cold card by its own choice. Each island pins one engine epoch, and one daemon hosts two epochs only as two separately pinned islands. The reason: the people who bear a reboot decide it, and a seat-holder who runs no hardware forces no one's restart. The ruling flips on a cadence act that must run unattended where a per-act unwrap cannot (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-231-* ''A realm's quorum and its boards'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-14). Each realm stands under ONE Nexus, which the vessel's first act there names and its edge ledger keeps; every reader takes the realm's quorum roster off that Nexus's charter, never off its own primary one; and the realm's boards key on the realm's own id, so a removal's record stays among its parties. The reason: authority comes from the governing charter while the record addresses the relation it affects. The ruling flips on a realm-native charter model with its own seat creation, migration and conflict rule (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/edge-hands">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-232-* ''A restore after guardian enrolment'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's own bundle restores after it enrols guardians, so long as the face's log still holds the set its own root enrolled by the typed first event and no later event moved it; a guardian rotation that moves the set cuts every earlier bundle off. The restored face stands provisional as the restore's key-history ruling holds. The reason: enrolling guardians must never silently kill a person's own backups, and the guardians' rotation, not the enrolment, cuts off a stolen bundle. The ruling flips on a provisional gate that cannot stop a restored face from signing an authority-changing act before a party confirms it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-restore">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:233:* ''Paper restores a root, never memory'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The split-root cards rebuild the persona root alone; content keys stay random and wrap under the vessel key or a bundle's own key, and no key the root derives opens memory. A person recovers memory through a bundle, under the route that bundle seals. The reason: a root card that opened memory would turn every share holder and every thief of the paper into a reader of the face's private bytes. The ruling flips on an explicit choice that root-share holders read memory, with the custody that choice costs stated.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-234-* ''A restore as persona zero'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A restore onto a fresh hearth runs through the founding act: the hearth founds a fresh one-seat seed charter, and the restored face stands as its persona zero and holds its new chair. A bundle's old chair claim carries no authority on the new hearth, since a bundle carries no seat key. A founding that stopped part way resumes only its own persona-zero root and its own seed charter, and refuses a root that differs from the restored one rather than minting over it. The reason: a person who lost their one machine meets their own face, never a second one. The ruling flips on a rule that a lost hearth's chair must survive, which would make a bundle carry seat authority it excludes.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-235-* ''A roll waits on its prior anchor'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-15). A seal roll refuses by name while the prior roll stands with no anchor, so no Nexus stacks a roll over a step its readers cannot yet carry across a removal. The reason: an admit carries across a seal roll only through its roll anchors, and a roll laid over an anchorless one strands every admit between them.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:236:* ''The working address'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A face's working document takes its id from a dedicated face address secret: 32 random bytes minted once per face, sealed on each of that face's vessels, delivered to a joining vessel by the fleet-join door, and moved only by a deliberate rotation act that opens a fresh working document; neither a per-Nexus key's re-issue nor a vessel key touches it. The id reads as the first 16 bytes of HMAC-SHA-256 keyed by that secret over the length-prefixed domain tag `lar/working-address/v1`, the wiki relation's stable id (the face's `wikiId`, never a recipe CID, a composition fingerprint or a label, so a recipe edit or a rename moves nothing), and the slot kind in its lowercase spelling (`draft`, `working` or `personal`; `temp` holds no document). Each working document starts empty, with no initial change, so two offline vessels of one face converge on one history; a vessel's first write lands as an ordinary change. The reason: two devices of one face open one notebook offline and sync into one, while a keyed id lets no observer link two faces or read the secret. The ruling flips on a face identity contract from train N that already names shared face-secret bytes with the same custody and rotation.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-237-* ''The admit's gate pin'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The admit carriage and fleet-join answer sign a validated full `GateBundlePin` for the hearth's sovereign sync route at the named Nexus, read by `readGateBundlePin`; its digest derives from that object. Dials index by (hearth, Nexus, route, tier). Floor routes receive their own full pins through an authenticated relation or a carried signed pin set; an announcement never authenticates its own first pin. The reason: a digest alone gives an offline dialer no trusted route or key. The ruling flips on an equally authenticated digest-to-full-pin carrier with an unambiguous route and offline first contact.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:238:* ''Frames after open'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A versioned sealed application header carries kind (`session`, `sync`, or a named control kind), message id, part index and count, total length, then bytes, only after the gate seat opens. Gate tags `0x01`–`0x13` serve the handshake alone. Reassembly and concurrent messages carry bounds; part size follows the Noise limit after header and sealing overhead. Missing, duplicate, mixed-kind, overlong and post-close parts refuse. The reason: a large sync frame needs bounded, unambiguous carriage. The ruling flips on a smaller measured layout that passes the same large-sync, replay, memory-bound and cross-kind vectors.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-239-* ''Sharing after the gate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). The proven same-operator class establishes transport alone. The session's proven face and scoped document view decide each document. A place arm reaches infrastructure alone; a PersonaGroup grant admits a sibling vessel of the same face and grants no blanket document access. Two tabs on one laptop wearing different faces see different books. The reason: transport kinship grants no document readership. The ruling flips on a scoped-view proof that another key carries the same face with exactly the same facets.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-240-* ''A device set aside'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). Each vessel face-key certificate binds its face key to its certified device edge. Before sorting a presentation as same-operator, the gate consults the fleet edge's shadow for that device edge and refuses while the mapping or fold reads unreadable. The wire carries only the face-scoped key. A restart and two-face witness gate the cutover. The reason: removal of a device must cut every face it wore. The ruling flips on causal withdrawal of every affected face certificate proven to reach every gate with no gap.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:241:* ''The contract seam'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). N2, N4 and N5 stand handed back. Train W owns the admit-carriage hunk of `nexus-contract.ts` for the cutover, keeps N's anchor and prior-roll checks, and lands the contract, `device-admit.ts`, fleet answer, verifier and vectors as one signed-shape change. The reason: one signature shape must cross every producer and reader together. The ruling flips on a proven independent carriage boundary that preserves those checks and signed bytes.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-242-* ''The founder's certificate'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). A founder self-issues its vessel face-key certificate through the checked issue door and withdrawal history a joiner uses. The reason: the founder's session needs the same chain and removal law. The ruling flips on a verified equivalent issue path with the same history.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:243:* ''Routes at the cutover'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). Walker arms, the sibling dial and the herm membership relay ship SHUT by name; H opens walkers with its live grant reader, W9 opens the sibling at face scope, and an explicit Nexus opens the herm relay. The oracle read face and reader convert where browser boot reads the oracle in production; elsewhere they ship SHUT by name after measuring `pullAndVerifyOracle`'s caller. The waystone reads the Nexus's one public answer before it trusts its engine. An untested old-wire fallback counts as open. The reason: a closed route grants no silent legacy authority. The ruling flips on a proven gate-native caller for each shut route.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:244:* ''The floor announcement'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). `waking-floor-announce` signs one canonical body per carried Nexus under that Nexus's floor bundle signing key: version, Nexus AID, floor route pin digest, floor standing and causal position. It travels only inside an authenticated socket or relay relation. The reader checks the already pinned floor pin, domain, Nexus, route and causal order, and treats the body as a peer hint alone. The reason: a floor hint must neither bootstrap its own trust nor replay across Nexuses. The ruling flips on a smaller body that still refuses cross-Nexus replay, stale replacement and first-contact self-certification.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-245-* ''Fleet join serves every face'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-15). `fleet join` names its face with `--face <index>`, default `0`; a nonzero face carries that face's certificates, grants and address secret. The reason: a person wears several faces, and each face needs its own fleet relation. The ruling flips on a face-independent proof that carries the same per-face authority without mixing identities.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-246-* ''A realm's steward map holds leaves'' (house ruling under the operator's delegation, 2026-10-16). The co-signed `keptBy` names fill `realmStewardMap`: each name a steward's worn per-Nexus face or a Handle, with the bags it keeps. That map answers which bags a steward keeps, never a root question; the realm consult's ROOT map stays `peerContractNymMap`, filled only by a root edge proven at the wire (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/two-maps">>). The reason: a leaf that answers a root question links the two maps the doctrine keeps apart. The ruling flips if a root edge proven at the reading seat comes to fill a realm map, which then stands beside this one under the root map's own name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-247-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:248:* ''The channel of intent'' (operator, 2026-10-20: //"Approve your leans, land the full models into the architecture now"//). The daemon wiki keeps working memory; a face's intents travel on that face's own intent plane, `@intents-<tag>`, a fifth face plane beside the four; a vessel's own records rest in its daemon bag, unmirrored; the face's pins rest in the face's custody and `@persona`. The approved leans: the plane stands from the first landing, never staged in the daemon bag; the winner reads by the intent's own preference list, else the lowest `H(atom ‖ intent id)`, and never elects; a single-effect fleet-wide verb never addresses "any device", and a human answer may name its executor; a claim never expires, a device's staleness stays a local suspicion, and the operator's release always wins; an `every` intent reaches a later-joined device unless its bound names a roster edge; a far agent reaches the plane through a relay seat, opt-in per face and ring-gated, its research before its build; an intent voids by supersession, a revoked delegation, a passed roster edge or the operator's cancel; compaction folds by the operator's act, never a timer; a local verb that touches its own vessel alone bypasses the plane and leaves its receipt in that vessel's bag. The plane carries a hand's decisions that cross devices, never its motion (the rubric, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">> #/the-rubric). Row `I1`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:249:* ''The place signer's fifth duty'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean). A place's finish at another place's gate, `GATE_PLACE_FINISH_DOMAIN`, joins the place signer's floor duties: a faceless place that reads another's floor performs a floor act. Each of the five duties binds its domain by an exact head at byte zero, in one table beside the allowlist; `X0` moves the framing into the signer.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-250-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:251:* ''Sync carries; verification decides'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">> and the controller's leans). A mutable CRDT carries identity claims and never decides them. Each face holds, on each device, a ''sealed identity anchor'' in its own custody (a D row): its PersonaGroup, its persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its device edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Only founding, admission and the recovery rites (guardian rotation, bundle restore, root cards) write an anchor; sync never writes one. Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed records in the face's `@persona` plane, a signed-entry log every reader verifies against the anchor and the KEL; two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner. The face planes hold verified projections. A device reads freely; an act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) checks the sealed frontier and refuses a target that names a newer bound, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under. Transparency and witnesses for equivocation wait for their own row. Wave C carries the build inside `K15` step 6.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-252-* ''Wave B's forks'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). A fresh PersonaGroup mints a fresh atom, never an orphan's seed. A tab reads its face's pins from its custody anchor before it opens its session, so the tab's own Repo retires; and each face holds its own social planes in the browser, keyed by PersonaGroup as on the node. Both ride Wave C with the anchor.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-253-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:254:* ''The order of the next waves'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans). Wave C (`K15` step 6 under the identity anchor) runs next, with `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 beside it on the floor's own ground, their composer hunks passing to the controller as patches, and slice 5 after it, since its accepted floor rests as a face's sealed row (a D row under the face's own FCK once Wave C lands); `I1` follows the anchor; the far agent's relay seat takes its own research after `I1`; `G37`'s renames ride `X0`'s bake; the sensorium resumes after `X0`, on the operator's word.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-255-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:256:* ''The edge frontier'' (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's leans after the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/edge-frontier-2026">>). Nothing signed today lets a reader tell a device never set aside from a raise erased or withheld, so the house adds a signed ''edge frontier'' per board, its own domain-separated certificate type, the persona KEL resolving its signer's key. Every hand that can raise on a board signs its own stream's frontier (a fleet board's root; a realm board's charter quorum, with its holder where vouch edges raise), and a frontier commits its counted acts through its boundary as a content-addressed snapshot, its parent frontier, and its roster and epoch lineage. A raise shadows its target at once for every reader that sees it, and counts toward widening once its signer registers it into the next frontier. Sync always carries acts, frontiers and snapshots. A widening act (admit, grant, a content key sealed or re-sealed to a reader) reads its target against a frontier of every raising hand that extends any head the reader pinned and includes every raise it has seen; it acts as of that frontier, its receipt naming it, and waits as unknown where none qualifies. Every fleet and realm founds with a signed empty genesis frontier, and an admit bundle carries the current frontier and its snapshot. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C, and the realm boards' leg landed with K17-R in PR #97. Row `K17`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-257-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-258-!!! The fresh start
