bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-274-* ''The multi-Nexus fold.'' A gate answers strangers if ANY Nexus it stands in reads OPEN. One gate key serves every Nexus a vessel carries, so this rule reduces exactly to per-Nexus posture once each Nexus carries its own wire key (R-WIRE) — not an interim.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-275-* ''Carriage keys on the guest's PROVEN leaf.'' A hearth-issued stub would read as a bearer capability to another guest's record and as a hearth-minted cross-lineage linker. The leaf already proves on every socket, so keying on it adds no linkage the hearth lacks; a fresh leaf opens a fresh carriage (#/open, carriage across leaves).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:276:* ''One store door.'' A command that touches the store runs inside the standing vessel over the owner-only socket, else owns the store itself for that moment. A second Repo beside a live holder writes bytes the replica never sees. `tools/direct-repo-witness.sh` names the two lawful `new Repo(` sites and reads any other as DRIFT.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-277-* ''No hearth-local deny set.'' Kapae and the roll suffice; a deny set would make a seizable list.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-278-* ''No node carriage.'' A node serves as its own durable store and no story walks its carriage; ruling N holds as a sorter property and W as the hearth's service. Node carry would open a new user story, never owed by N or W.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-284-* ''The carriage verifier holds the root'': it checks the epoch, the signature AND a subject root it holds locally, and refuses by name without that root.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-285-* ''Guardian placement'' reads as advice the house names at enrolment, never a refusal. ''QR pairing'' shows a check string on both screens after the channel opens.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:286:* ''The floor vessel key drops its next-key commitment'', inside the one identity train. It changes the vessel's signed inception bytes; the operator may overturn it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-287-* ''A long-silent fleet device'' catches up before it acts: a presentation carries its presenter's frontier of the face's withdrawal history, and a gate that holds a later one answers `unconfirmed` and hands over what the device lacks. No clock; a house reading the operator may overturn (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-withdrawal-proof">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-288-* ''The strangers' dial drops the NEWEST arrival'' when its slots fill; a slot frees by the operator's answer or a roll.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-290-* ''A restarted always-on node serves no hosted phone until a human unlocks.'' The resolver and the terminator keep answering, so the page loads and the sync waits; the page says so in one line, until the ember lands.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-291-* ''A crossing gets recorded, never interior life.'' Only an authority, vessel, federation or externally meaningful crossing becomes distributed canon (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/mandate-activity-provenance">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:292:* ''A package names no vessel.'' Every entity starts at the herm floor; a seated persona lights the Lararium stack over it. Only a lararium lights a Pronaos, and a herm mirrors a house's published bytes by CID (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/pronaos#/the-placement">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-293-* ''Deferred by the house'': realm feeding (two carriers disagree on max over per-writer slots against a blank merge; it waits for the first-realm arc), community exit, and funding, where payment may buy capacity and never standing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-294-
