bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-355-!!! 4 · KAHU PLANE ~ the realms, the signer, and the one AID train
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-356-Build order: the realm and signer shapes against the rulings; then R-CHARTER, the one train that moves
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:357:identity bytes; then R-WIRE, so every pin changes once.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-358-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-359-* ''Realms'': a vessel stands one plane per realm, and a verb names its realm (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/many-realms">>). A cabal reads as its relation closure and takes no key or roster of its own. A cabal realm's documents cross between two operators once the realm's member consult answers for a peer.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:360:* ''The steward signer'': the worn face or a quorum Handle, never the root (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm#/the-steward-signer">>). The seal, the fold and the steward door stand in code; the composing vessel's `realm-bag` verb takes the door through the compose owner's hand. The docker `meme` scenario then proves it by hand at "B edits, promotes", in the asker's order: B asks to keep the bag with her worn face, and A consents.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:361:* ''Thresholded admission and promotion'' stand built: the chartered classes derive from the charter's own seats and threshold (`chartered-classes.ts`); promotion approves the exact bytes' hash with purpose, surface, class and epoch (`promotion-approval.ts`, `lares nexus promote open|sign|check`); Kahu-cabal admission stands as its own act at the high-impact threshold, where a vouch admits nobody (`kahu-cabal-admission.ts`, `lares nexus cabal`) (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/chartered-classes">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-362-
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-363-''R-CHARTER, the one AID train.'' Its first stage stands landed (train K of #/the-trains): the chairs sign with seat keys of their own and pre-rotate on cold cards, a Nexus answers to `nexus-<sha>`, the floor key founds by a clockless self-signed inception (its next cold key committed since `W29`), per-Nexus keys mint at random, the PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, and the Stable founding act founds a hearth (`lares vessel found --hearth`): the place, persona zero and a PRIVATE seed charter at one seat, with no keyring, every fleet relation bound to that charter's AID, and every harness that founds a hearth founding through it (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook#/found">>). What stays owed:
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-372-* One client dial per (hearth, Nexus), so a vessel walks at more than one hearth; until then a second walk hearth refuses aloud.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-373-* The vessel key stops linking a walker's leaves across Nexuses on the wire (`two-maps` clause 5's residual), and the oracle pointer's vessel-key correlation goes with it (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/pronaos#/the-rung-ladder`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:374:* ''Per-dial transport keys on the sibling channel'': a leaf proves to a herm under a key fresh per dial, and the leaf-peer transcript binds that key in place of the device key the relay stamps, so a herm colluding with a revoked leaf reads no sibling's device key off its own gate (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/identity-slot-policy#/the-persona-group-secret`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:375:* ''The admit signature the build owes'': the canon-document list and full sovereign sync `GateBundlePin` enter the signed bytes through the fleet answer and admit carriage; `device-admit.ts` mints the internal `device-admit/v1` edge. The browser's first proof rides `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-376-* ''Owed (b), the knock tests offline'': the knock path computes an HMAC-derived segment (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`); an observer holding candidate keys tests a sniffed knock offline, so not echoing the key protects only against an observer with no candidates.
