bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-395-!!! The sealed store ~ five steps threaded through the paths (operator-approved model; step one's format stands as law and in code; each later step lands in its place before the fence, under #/the-attractor's ruling)
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-396-''Step three's launch kit'': <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/docs/train-s3-launch">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:397:* ''The model'': cleartext lives in the live wiki and in the operator's projected files alone. A private bag rests as authenticated ciphertext chunks, the same bytes at rest and in a blind carrier's hands; a node that holds the capability and stands locked rests sealed. Private bytes take randomized authenticated encryption addressed over the ciphertext, so convergent sealing leaves the private tier. A bag's content key rolls at a causal removal act, never by a clock.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-398-* ''Scope'' (operator ruling): the sealing covers the wiki content stores, node and browser, and the content-addressed store, in carriage as well as at rest. The memory palace, the sensorium, receipts and logs stand outside it. Public and crossroads content stays readable to whoever holds the public keys or lookups.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-399-* ''Faces stand as facets of one operator'' (operator steer): no per-face projection root. Each kind of reader gets named — own vessel, own facet, a friend's face, a hosted guest, a carrier that holds none — before any admission-history rule gets written. One tree on disk serves the person: a projected wiki stands as a surface a session leases, and an edit from disk returns under that session's face (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>). Whoever holds the disk reads every facet's projection and may link them.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:400:* ''Step 1, the one private-byte format'': it stands as law at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store">>, and that carrier names each part the code holds: the sealed value with its ciphertext address and named refusals; the key version, manifest and checkpoint records; the lockbox payload; shareable-history spans; the key lineage and the roll a seat roll feeds. The content-addressed store and the walker's carriage seal and open through it, no opener returns unauthenticated bytes, and no key derives from content or from a Nexus secret. The format changes ONCE, there. The content-key roll stands subscribed to the daemon island's seat rolls. What steps two to five take from the format reads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:401:* ''Step 2, the key's seat'': a content key's lockbox, the store that rests lockboxes, records and the chunk index, and the content-key holder stand as law at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/the-store">>, and that carrier names each part the code holds. A node vessel's daemon island seats the holder beside its Keyhive identities and subscribes the content-key roll to its own seat rolls; a removal's successor wraps for the readers that remain, each lockbox into a Keyhive document of its own, so a removed device opens nothing a vessel seals after it counts the raise. Owed from this step, each to its owner: the session open that hands the island a signer and the chain check, without which no content key mints on a production vessel; a door from the island to the vessel's fold for the raises it counts; the face join's call for a from-now admission or a hand-over; and the browser shore's rest and Archive writer. A raise over the vessel that founded a face's key group names no seat a roll can leave out, so that vessel keeps its keys until `K12` stands a fresh group. What steps three and four take from this step reads at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed">>.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:402:* ''Step 3, after ONE FACE'': sealed storage values and hydration scoped by the session's face; every fetch, write, catalog lookup and content-addressed read gets checked against that face, since a key alone cannot stop a trusted daemon handing one face another's document.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-403-* ''Step 4, after the KAHU PLANE's seats and wire'': sealed history published to and fetched from a blind carrier by the house's own carriage protocol, with a causal index. A carrier never joins document sync.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-404-* ''Step 5, after ONE FACE'': a public bag served at the floor of a locked node; today the floor serves the oracle snapshot alone.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-448-!!! Seven-league stride notes
