bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:450:* ''Integrity owed: face isolation, end to end'' (`K15` step 3, `B1`; `F6`'s slice three rides here with Wave B). Its witness: one adversarial multi-tab, multi-face run in a real browser, an unadmitted port, a stale generation, a cross-face sealed write and the last session's lock, where today only fake islands read them. MEASURED (the fresh read of Wave B; the readers, 2026-10-20). Wave B (PR #81) builds the guards and their reds on fake islands and the node; the real-browser adversarial run waits on Wave C's one SharedWorker per house.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:451:* ''Integrity owed: identity authority enforced, beyond the prose'' (`K15` step 6). Its witness: Wave C's red suite, a forged selector and a coherent foreign bundle refused, one sequence signed twice surfacing as a fork, a frontier that never falls. LEAD on the suite's shape; MEASURED that today's gate verifies continuity alone (`boot-daemon-keyhive.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-452-* ''Integrity owed: rowless threads take ids.'' The carried threads on this shelf with no row id (title-to-path persistence, live equivocation's prerequisites, the crossing record's membrane and rail, the antigen share's lapse, realm standing across operators, the smaller threads) mint ids, so a lane can schedule and witness each.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:453:* ''Research pair: the far agent's relay seat'' (`I1`'s relay phase). Its question: the least relay trust and attestation that stops capability escalation and argument substitution while keeping causal provenance. Lenses: protocol security / distributed failure semantics.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-454-
