bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-466-* `F10` A person's fleet view and removal; the long-silent device rule of #/decisions. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-467-* `F11` The hands: the watcher as a leasing session, the seat under a standing grant, the Mask as a record field, door parity at the session (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract#/the-hands">>). An agent's dissent drafts and a person's direct ask edits (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:468:* `K12` A fresh PersonaGroup for a seat no hand can revoke (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/keys">>). The PersonaGroup stands as a Keyhive group, so every other seat's revocation rolls the bags the group reaches (`persona-group-roll`); revoke authority follows the seating lineage, so a seat whose seating hand left, and the founder's own seat, leave only by a fresh group. Owed first: a name the face keeps across groups, since its plane names key on the group's id. It builds inside `K15`'s per-face removal step. K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-469-* `S7` Standing leans the seal met, kept as built unless the operator overturns one: an unlock mints a fresh Keyhive document for a binding whose floor-minted document died; one contact card per stand; the browser's creator veil stays unwired; a browser founded before the Keyhive move refuses to boot. Answered by rule and still open: a resumed face founding mints a new group; a founding stopped before its anchors re-founds with a fresh veil.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-470-* `H5` An invited user's root mints on her device, sealed; the herm carries a sealed copy. B.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-477-* The crossing rail's three requirements (both ends as presented capabilities, a saga shape, declared deletion semantics) and a realm tally's move onto the shared substrate both stand researched and unbuilt.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-478-* A deny-only antigen share wants entries that can lapse, carried provenance and a merge rule before two lists ever merge.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:479:* Realm standing does not cross operators: a feed slot lands in its writer's own daemon bag. The cure points the realm verbs' store at the realm's shared substrate and requires the seal on a foreign slot; the seal verifier holds no caller yet (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/cabal-realm-clock.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-480-* Smaller threads: the tombstone and whiteout verb, reserved; Automerge history growth; `lares wiki` subcommands that print for humans alone; an engine-swap reconcile that answered `current` against a stale engine; the NFC assertion at the ingest shore; the parser's retired typed-edge emission plane (`kumu-device.ts`); a `TimeoutNegativeWarning` in e2e runs, unlocalized; the house's register names ahi kā Hawaiian where its documented home reads Māori, and a primary source should settle it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-481-* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. Owed to `K18`: a closed roster's keys can still raise the lease (stale more, never less) until the recovery door closes that window; the fold never lowers.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:482:* `K18` The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation of a persona root beneath its KEL prefix, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the current `@persona` log and signed frontier. Owed: no production door rotates a root today, and the ceremony waits on the guardian count, an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`); `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function (Wave C, <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane">> #/owed). K.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:484:* `P1` The steward signer: the composing vessel's `realm-bag` verb calls the steward door (`realm-steward.ts`); the docker `meme` scenario by hand, in the asker's order; a door for a collective Handle's seal waits on the chartered classes; the vouch door, the feed's writer and a realm's holder hand sign with the worn face's key at the Nexus the realm stands under (`cabal-face.ts`). P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-485-* `P9` The re-seal proof and the fork-resolve act stand ruled (#/rulings): the re-seal record builds with sealed-store step three, the fork-resolve act in train N.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:486:* `P13` Per-meme grants; a leaf honouring a session's effective recipe. O1 for the recipe.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:487:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-488-* `W9` The sibling channel at face scope, on per-dial transport keys. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:489:* `W12` The herm route for cancel and the three receipts, as ruled (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/receipt-ledger#/the-relay-leg">>); no code asks, cancels or answers across a herm. Owed, with `W9`: the ask, the cancel and the vessel's answer as a tagged inner frame under the sealed sibling session's own seal, the vessel reading that session's proof as the asker's; the herm's bare delivery note inside the session, bound to the ask's unique request id and the session's causal position, attesting transit and never execution; and the rule for which verbs a sibling's standing reaches across the session (`sibling-channel.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-490-* `E2` The serving key's custody and its unattended road (#/rulings, the ember's key at rest; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Built: the fifth class `serving` in the carrier table, read by the census and `vault status`; SK minted at the founding; `sk-slots` with the vessel key's entry, opened at every human unlock and re-wrapped by a vessel-key rotation. Owed: the serving rows under SK and SK's own rotation; no minting secret in any serving row; the anchor path, where an ember slot answers unattended only against a hardware-sealed hearth key whose attestation the ember checks on each ask; the confirm path, where every slot of a hearth with no such anchor answers only on a person's confirm and threshold two asks a second confirm, never an unattended raise; and the bare deny-only `sk-rotation-owed` mark that any counted removal sets and that refuses every ask until SK rolls (`vault-carriers.ts`, `keyslot.ts`, `custody-seat.ts`). E.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-491-* `E3` The serving gate's tier (#/rulings, the ember's serving gate; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-gate-exchange">>). Owed: a third tier name in the route type, its bundle derived from SK under its own registered domain, its pin, and a pin's move by a signed causal event or a verified key-history step alone, with no quiet period that ages a pin out (`gate-bundle.ts`). E.
