bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:506:* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-507-* ''Research pair: the Keyhive substrate's contract'' (`W11`, filed after the seat). Its question: which substrate properties stand as contract and which shift by version, each needing a guard at run time. Lenses: dependency contract analysis / adversarial compatibility testing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:508:* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`; its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake). MEASURED (two traded rounds, then a Mu test on the web, 2026-10-26; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading): IK already stands, so a dialer proves itself before any verdict; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; on the sovereign route a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path learns which of the K gates sharing an address and route a dial selects, at most log2(K) bits per dial, never the face, the verdict or a sealed byte; no public-pin filter escapes that, and a secret selector costs per-Nexus key delivery and a causal re-key on every removal. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) that the sovereign promise leaves a pin-holding path reader outside it, so `W10` closes as a named leak, with more research owed later.
