bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-523-* `K9` The cadence lineage's seat events and its offer verifier; the joint founding's one cadence citation stands, and a household seed cites none (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu#/contract">>). P, with the offers.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-524-* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout stands frozen (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-frozen-frames): six tags in two direction blocks, a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none, fixed body and subject bounds and 65-byte finish and verdict frames, witnessed by `gate-frame-freeze.test.ts`. The gate answers an upgrade only after its first flight decrypts (`FaceGate.preflight`), so a flight no bundle opens draws a destroyed socket before any 101. No wire byte moved. Built, PR #96. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:525:* `W29` The place signs by a scoped signer under a pre-rotated KEL (#/rulings, the place signs by a scoped signer, 2026-10-19; kit <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w29-place-kel-lane">>): built, PR #98, 2026-10-26. One KEL grammar (`vessel-kel.ts`, beside `persona-kel` and `handle-kel`): the inception seats the online signer and commits a cold next-key digest; a rotation reveals that key, which signs it, seats a replacement signer and commits a fresh next key; no interaction events. Every founding door, node, hearth, herm kindle and browser alike, mints the armed inception and lands no byte before the founding card reads back through the `PlaceFoundingCard` port, and the cold seed rests on no file. `lares vessel rotate` runs the card ceremony: it verifies the old card against the head, reads the replacement card back, then stages, publishes and reconciles under one custody claim, and a restart never invents a successor. Peers learn the head from the Nexus carriage board and an offline herm from the carry bundle; one fold, bounded at 64 rows and 8 pieces of fork evidence per AID, refuses a gap, a rollback and a fork. The five floor duties sign and verify `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage`. A seed census names every raw-seed consumer and fails on a new one. Owed: a browser ceremony UI that seats a card (until it lands, the browser's KEL door refuses by name and a browser leaf holds no place KEL); the duty verifiers resolving their signer at the head (`verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`), with `W14`–`W16`; the seed's other reach, K15's bonds, named in the census. W.
