bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-570-* `A9` The browser harness keeps a read-only repository bind; a Playwright harness image retires it. B.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:571:* `A10` The Pronaos household proof: one reserved docker project that attributes the arrival bytes to their shore and the node faces to their owners, then fresh browser peers through relay and oracle loss. A.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-572-* `A11` A pushed head of this branch whose held-out reading shows every driver green (`node tools/ci-verdict.mjs`, the third reading). A.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:573:* `A12` An unlock spends its time in three boots of the wiki engine, and the terminal shows nothing meanwhile. One instrumented run on a marked scratch root, pinned to one core, with the genesis corpus alone: the key derivation takes under two seconds; the sovereign composition then takes about six to reach `corpus-ready`, seven from the `[dyad]` line to the daemon island's `working layer attached`, and four to `tw5-booted`. An unlock sent while the floor's own daemon island still boots waits that boot out first, six seconds more, so the first unlock after a restart answered in twenty-eight seconds where a later one answered in fifteen. The span a person met past eighty seconds sits at the same `[dyad]` line, so it scales with the corpus the daemon island boots over. No small cure reads here. Owed: a progress line per phase at the unlocking terminal, and a measurement over a full workspace corpus. The compose owner's boot path. A.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-574-* `A13` A staged container that restarts after its boot's founding act wrote the seed charter and before it lit persona zero's face loses the staged card: the next boot's act completes the face, the charter already stands, so no card returns, and the kahu roll under `LAR_STAND_KAHU` skips with its warning (`tools/lararium-container-boot.sh`, the `LAR_STAND_FACE` founding and the roll after it). It binds disposable staged roots alone: a household founding prints its card on the terminal and keeps no copy. A.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-575-* `K8` The face-proof gate reads the admitted key's hand-over line, as the socket gate does. The key and its line stand built: a face's per-Nexus key mints at random into its sealed row and re-issues by a hand-over the carriage board carries (`nexus-leaf.ts`, `lares persona reissue`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-key-hierarchy">>). The remainder rides the socket cutover. W.
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-579-* `P3` Many realms: the cross-operator member consult of a cabal realm waits on the face-scoped proof subject and on the vouch door naming a worn face's key. P, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-580-* `P8` One public answer per Nexus, signed by the steward: the floor release answer, built as `W26`'s release slice (#/rulings, 2026-10-18): the body, the steward's seal, the approval and the porch stand (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/kahu">> #/floor-release). The domain's Handle table stays here, off the ceremony's chain by ruling. P, W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:581:* `P17` The realm feed's writer check: the feed verb runs in the daemon island (`cabal-realm-verbs.ts`), while the worn face's key at a realm's Nexus mints on the vessel's main thread behind the custody door (`cabal-face.ts`), so the verb resolving its own writer needs a door from the island to the vessel, the shape of `dyad:ask`, which moves the capability inventory and the compose files. The one production caller, `lares cabal feed`, names that key through `cabal-face`; the residue: a caller that types any writer. P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:582:* `P18` The shared-canon read consults `kahuCabalCanonAccess`, admission AND sentinel membership; until it does, a removed group keeps its Keyhive sentinel capability at every reader but that one (`boot-daemon-keyhive`). Both vessels' daemon payloads (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`) carry the group and sentinel ids alone, so each composition threads the Nexus AID, the seated roster and the carriage board into the read together; a node-only gate leaves the browser reader open. P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-583-* `P19` Cabal acts across a roll: an act counts only under the epoch it names, so after a seal roll standing reads `absent` until the seats re-admit at the new head; anchored ancestry, which `lares nexus members` reads, carries them, and an `onRolled` refold for the cabal verbs follows once a live reading folds them. It lands with `P20`, under the same writer rule. P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:584:* `W10` The knock tests offline for a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): CLOSED as a named leak by the operator's ruling (2026-10-26), the sovereign route's promise leaving a pin-holding path reader outside it (face-proof #/named-leaks; the reading at `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` #/the-knock-reading). More research owed later: whether a secret selector, its first-dial bootstrap and its causal re-key on every removal earn their cost, read again when a sovereign pin escapes its members' custody, when route confidentiality against pin-holders enters the promise, or when hearths commonly stand many Nexuses behind one address; a flip after `X0` moves the dial's URL bytes by its own versioned rite. W, canon.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-585-* `W11` Keyhive keeps the PersonaGroup's private membership and carries no face chain: four probe readings on 0.3.0-alpha.1 stand as alarms (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/face-chain-substrate.probe.test.ts`), and a Keyhive bump re-reads them. House. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-586-* `W17` Face switching on one device, and a second joined face on one vessel. House. W.
