bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-589-* `W22` `composeCasTransits` in `node-cas.ts` shapes `P10`'s client leg and gets wired; `openBrowserVessel`'s `walkInvite` option stands without a caller, while the CLI's `walkInvite` runs `walk invite`. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-590-* `W23` The floor-crossing CI cell (`packages/lararium-web` `vitest.crossing.config.ts`, about seven minutes under chromium) reads the browser floor crossing on every push: the `floor-crossing` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs it under a scratch HOME, LAR_ROOT and LAR_STAGE_DIR, and `tools/vitest-config-callers.test.mjs` fails any named vitest config that no workflow, tool or package script runs. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:591:* `W24` `herm-reshares-public-blob` walks a public user book (PR #55): the fleet mints `herm-public-photo` on A and registers it public on the realm; step ③ LOADs the blob into the book's working slot and promotes it into canon by `MOVE` through the island `W27` opens; step ④ reads C, a second vessel of A's own face joined by `fleet join`, listing the book with A's doc id through its stood realms; steps ⑤b and ⑦ name an unstaged blob, and ⑦'s shut holds. Owed beside: readiness entries (a wiki mounted with its layers laid) and a per-carrier entry, so a script awaits a second write too; the daemon's reach waits on a bag's document the way the kernel's slot wait does, instead of one bounded find; a guard on the event route's order; a CLI that gives up on its budget cancels its waiter. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:592:* `F1` The scoped document view stands specified in mesh (`session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`); the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`) and the island kernel's half ride it, and no production caller mounts a surface. Owed: every interactive surface mounts under it in place of the broad sync port, which waits on a verified face (train W) and on callers that hold a session (`F4`, `F6`); the share verdict's caller keeps an owner from offering a session island a document beyond its facets; an admitted leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon documents, and the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves (`hearth-canon.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `open-node-vessel.ts`); a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-593-* `F2` One recipe resolver (`surface-recipe.ts`) and the pool keyed by the whole session key (`mountSurface`) stand specified in mesh, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. Both platforms select plugins through its `resolveRecipePluginCids`; no production caller reaches `resolveSurfaceRecipe`. Owed: the node and browser compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount; the wiki door (`mountWiki`), its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller; a surface island's events reach a verb gate bound to its session (`onSurfaceEvent`) when the node callers move (`F4`). O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:594:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-595-* `F8` The control-event leg stands built: `lar:control-event` and `lar:control-result` replace `wiki:dom-event` and `wiki:dom-input` (`lar-camera.ts`, `projection-sink.ts`). Owed to the o-takiage: burned-name guard assertions in `lar-wire.test.ts` and `projection-input-leg.test.ts`. O1.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:596:* `F9` The switch; the vessel-wide selector retires. Its one persisted shape, the selector's two stores (the node's active-persona index and the browser's `ACTIVE_PERSONA_STORE`), retired with `K15` Wave D (PR #95): the worn face lives as session state on node and browser, and no store keeps it. The switch act itself lands additive. O1.
