bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-662-* `P20` The carriage gates (`carriage-board.ts`, `vessel-raise.ts`, `nexus-carriage.ts`) count at the head alone, while `lares nexus members` honours anchored ancestry, so the list can show a member a gate does not yet honour. Built (PR #50): the carrier folds read the anchored lineage, and the contract writer cites the carried heads it supersedes across epochs for both families, so an uncarry, a roll and a re-carry read in order. Built (PR #54): a gate verifies a place contract carried across a charter roll in either direction, a newer gate walking the arm's roll anchors and an older gate accepting the presenter's charter epochs only where they extend its held lineage and pass `verifySealLineage`, each failing closed without its proof; the presenter assembles both, and `readBoardPresentation` folds with ancestry. The herm-mesh and mesh-scenarios witnesses join after A's boot roll. The held-out cell `herm-mesh-roll` (PR #57) rolls A's charter between two herm joins after the boot serves, each herm naming its own head, and presents the opening carry at the rolled head twice: under A's own roll anchor it verifies, and under the same anchor parts signed outside the seats it falls silent by place-contract name. P19's cabal half stays parked on `--gate-ancestry`. P.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:663:* `W18` The founding hearth's carriage fold walks the roll anchors (PR #50): after a charter roll, the carrier folds at the carriage pull's refresh, `placeCarriedNexuses`, the membership refold and the carry-bundle take count every act the anchored lineage carries, and count none without an anchor (`carriageAncestryFromBoard`; red and controls in `carrier-fold-across-roll.test.ts`). Held-out herm-mesh and the nexus cell then read A filing all four pins and verifying relay-2, and with `P20`'s gate half (PR #54) both read green. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-664-* `W21` A joinee mounts the hearth's `@lararium` corpus read-only beside its own, while the oracle plane never crosses (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Each vessel's pointers rest in its own `@catalog` (PR #52), so a joined vessel's pointer no longer replaces its hearth's, and `shared-oracle-doc.probe` holds that two synced vessels each keep their own. The rest rides `W26`'s floor slices: a joinee reads its hearth's floor by the release and its CIDs (slice 4), where slice 5's accept act moves its pin; a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until Wave C's face context carries the charter and the board to it, and `device-admit.ts` states the law. W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:665:* `W25` The carried bag event names its creator in the clear, where the WHO plane's veil-born group hides it: measured red (`packages/lararium-keyhive/tests/bag-event-creator.probe.test.ts`, lane `--w26-own-canon`); `K15`'s step 2 hides it, since no vessel-wide identity then creates a face's bag (#/rulings, 2026-10-16 and 2026-10-18). W.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:666:* `W27` A write reaches its wiki's working layer (#/rulings, 2026-10-18). Built (PR #55): `LOAD` into a canon bag refuses, naming the promotion it owes, while genesis and founding seed through their own named door; an act aimed at a bag opens the bag's own wiki, its recipe record or the floor, through one mesh record-or-floor export the surface recipe and the node's open and act paths share, and lands in its working slot; a mount that cannot stand refuses by its cause; the daemon wiki keeps the daemon's own reach. `W24` walks it. W.
