bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-869-# ''Rulings that rest in their own carriers'': the promotion receipt's fields (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/canon-boundary">>), the one-of-one mantle (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/handle-card">>), the lease's questions (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/realm-bag-brief">>), and the offering's questions (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/heraldry">>).
--
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-871-# ''Alerts and shadows.'' Whether a disk conflict that arrives while no wiki stands pinned raises its alert at the next pin; whether a hand that deletes its override of a shadow leaves a delete, where today the shadow's text gets saved as a record; whether the page warns when a browser has joined no face.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem-872-# ''The confirm door upstream.'' The fork asks its questions through the wiki itself (`$tw.utils.confirm`, `tm-confirm`). Owed before a donation: the order of actions after a confirm, a switch for a blocking prompt, and one squashed change. The withdrawn render boundary's upstream pull request, if it still stands open, advertises a design the fork backed out.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:873:# ''One sentence for the `CLAUDE.md` adapter note'', the operator's to place: the CLI's ingest, watch and REPACK derive against `LAR_BAGS` and `LAR_WIKIS`, so "read neither" holds for the daemon's projection mirrors alone.
